Namely, if $E$ is derived complete and $a : K \to E$ is a map, then the commutative diagram <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ K \ar[r]_ a \ar[d] &  E \ar[d]^{\cong } \\  K^\wedge \ar[r]^{a^\wedge } &  E^\wedge }  \]
</div> shows that any map into $E$ factors through $K^\wedge $. Choose a distinguished triangle $K \to K^\wedge \to C$ and apply ${}^\wedge $. We find that $C^\wedge = 0$. By the above this means that $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (C, E) = 0$ for $E$ derived complete and this proves that $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K, E) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K^\wedge , E)$ as desired.